This repository implements its own Rust/Python code. It does **not** copy
substantial source from third-party projects. Behavior, APIs, and test oracles
were inspected as follows:

Reference inspected (behavior / architecture only — not copied):

- pysam-developers/pysam — Python API shape, 0-based half-open fetch, count /
  count_coverage / pileup filters, VariantFile field names.
- victormar1/rubam — BAM analytics performance baseline (chunking, depth /
  pileup). Used for runtime/RSS comparison, not as a source drop-in.
- zaeleus/noodles — Rust-native BAM/CRAM/VCF codecs via the `noodles` crate
  dependency (upstream crate, not vendored).
- samtools / HTSlib / bcftools — CLI oracles (`view`, `depth`, `index`) and
  CRAM fixture generation (`samtools view -C`).

If substantial third-party code is ever transplanted, record license,
attribution, and the source commit here before merge.
